.TH FINANCE-RECEIPT-SYNC 1 "2026-11-09" "Finance Infrastructure" "Nexus Host Utilities"
.SH NAME
finance-receipt-sync \- project validated iPhone-scanned receipts into finance analytics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/data/bin/finance-receipt-sync
.RB [ --preview | --apply ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the existing Receipt Wrangler PostgreSQL records and protected normalized
submission archives. Requires a unique exact date, total, merchant, linked-item
and item-amount match, then verifies quantity, unit price, subtotal, tax,
discounts and total. A distinct existing email receipt with the same merchant,
date and total is held for review rather than counted twice.
.PP
The default
.B --preview
performs no writes and prints aggregate counts only.
.B --apply
inserts only new, validated rows into the existing
.B purchase_receipts
and
.B receipt_items
finance analytics tables. Source identity is unique by
.B (source, source_key)
and the source archive hash is checked on subsequent runs. Ambiguous and
changed sources fail closed. The script does not change Receipt Wrangler,
Wealthfolio, mailbox state or bank transactions.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Nexus host Python 3.9+, Docker CLI/daemon, live
.B receipt-wrangler-db-1
and
.B finance-analytics-db
PostgreSQL containers, and root read access to
.B /opt/homelab-api/receipt-intake/submitted
(mode 0700 with 0600 JSON archives). The existing encrypted finance-analytics
PostgreSQL backup must be verified before applying changes.
.SH OUTPUT
Only aggregate counts and generic errors are printed. Financial details stay
in the existing protected databases and archives. Exit status 0 means preview
or apply/readback completed; nonzero means stop and review, not retry blindly.
.SH ROLLBACK
Identify records by source
.B wrangler_scan
and the protected source-key/hash in the analytics database. Review intervening
changes and referenced matches, then remove only this run's added rows with a
targeted transaction. Do not restore an old whole database over new owner data.
The source and this manual are owned by the private
.B iragonforce/ops
repository.
